    /// The shared state. Members ask again, with `after`, as soon as each answer arrives, while waiting, on details and in the player.
    ///
    /// Plain HTTP long polling, so every client can follow along, Roku
    /// included. With `after`, the answer waits until `version` passes it
    /// or the Watch together ends, at most 25 seconds, then answers the
    /// state as it stands; without, it answers at once. Each poll by a
    /// member marks that member present; a member unseen for 30 seconds is
    /// not present, and a Watch together none of whose members has polled
    /// for 60 seconds ends.
    ///
    /// Every play, pause and seek takes effect on both members at one
    /// instant, `effectiveAtMs`, a lead after it was sent: from then the
    /// player is at `effectivePositionMs`, advancing while `playing`. The
    /// lead is what the slowest present member needs to hear of the change
    /// and act on it, at least 0.3 second and at most 1 second; it need
    /// not be a whole second, and a client must not assume one. A member
    /// says what it needs with `rttMs` and `floorMs` on each poll and each
    /// action, and one that sends neither, as a client written before them
    /// does, needs the full second. A client
    /// estimates its offset from the server's clock from the
    /// `serverTimeMs` of a few answers without `after`, taking the one
    /// with the shortest round trip as answered at its midpoint. A change
    /// whose instant is still ahead is applied at that instant on the
    /// client's estimate of the server's clock, the sender's own player
    /// included; one already past is applied at once at the position it
    /// has run on to. While playing, a player more than 0.5 seconds from
    /// the shared position seeks to it. A member who is not in the player
    /// opens it, and starts its own playback session at the shared
    /// position, when `playing` turns true. `version` rises with every
    /// change. Only the household's profiles that may see its title see
    /// it; others get 404. A member who may no longer see the title gets
    /// 404 too, and it ends for the other.
    ///
    ///
    /// - Remark: HTTP `GET /watch-together/{watchTogetherId}`.
    /// - Remark: Generated from `#/paths//watch-together/{watchTogetherId}/get(getWatchTogether)`.
    func getWatchTogether(_ input: Operations.GetWatchTogether.Input) async throws -> Operations.GetWatchTogether.Output
    /// Leave, or cancel while waiting. It ends for both; the other's next poll reads ended and plays on alone.
    ///
    /// - Remark: HTTP `DELETE /watch-together/{watchTogetherId}`.
    /// - Remark: Generated from `#/paths//watch-together/{watchTogetherId}/delete(leaveWatchTogether)`.
    func leaveWatchTogether(_ input: Operations.LeaveWatchTogether.Input) async throws -> Operations.LeaveWatchTogether.Output
