    /// Starts playing an item for a profile on this device.
    ///
    /// The request carries the full current capability snapshot, never a
    /// reference to a stored one. The server builds an ordered plan and
    /// answers with the entry in use and its stream.
    ///
    /// A song plays as an audio-only session with the same plan model and
    /// no quality menu: no rungs, no previews, a negotiated width and
    /// height of 0, and audioCodec and lossless set. At home a song the
    /// client can play is copied as it is, else converted to AAC at
    /// 256 kb/s. Away from home a lossless song converts to AAC at 256 kb/s
    /// and a lossy one is copied. On a metered or low-data path every song
    /// is AAC at 128 kb/s. A kid starting a song or YouTube video their
    /// filter hides gets 404.
    ///
    /// The session plays one edition of the item, editionId or else the
    /// default, and the server picks its file: of the edition's copies,
    /// the one whose plan starts with the cheapest verdict (direct play,
    /// remux, audio transcode, video transcode), then the tallest picture
    /// the display shows, then HDR the display keeps, then the least
    /// picture beyond the display, then the higher bitrate. A copy holding
    /// audioTrackId or subtitleTrackId is taken outright. The session's
    /// mediaFileId names the file picked. An editionId of another item
    /// answers 404; an edition without files answers 409.
    ///
    /// Only files on disk when the call is made are picked from, whatever
    /// MediaFile.missingAt says: a file found there loses its mark and one
